{
  "_comment": "Hand-kept inventory of AlpacaCore/external/ for scripts/dependency_snapshot.py. 'sdks': one entry per vendored package (path, name, version, source of the version; version null = none exists in the tree, so the purl carries none; sha256 = digest of the git-tracked files under path, written by `dependency_snapshot.py --pin`; optional updates = where scripts/dependency_updates.py looks for a newer version: provider release-page (url, a regex whose first group is the version) or json (url, dotted path to a list, match, field)). 'documents': upstream documents and reference sources a driver is built from, watched by dependency_updates.py (provider github-file: the newest commit on repo/file; hash: sha256 of the document, an HTML page's visible text; page: the highest version a regex matches; github-release: the repository's latest release); 'baseline' is the reviewed value, and a changed upstream opens an issue until a PR sets the baseline to it. 'path' is the local copy, if any (--check fails when it is missing). 'no_upstream': docs-only directories with no upstream to watch, each with its reason. 'system_libraries': libraries the build takes from Debian (debian/control), with their upstream GitHub repo and the version Debian trixie ships as baseline; dependency_updates.py reports an upstream release newer than the baseline. An 'updates' block may name a static 'changelog' URL, and a json source a 'changelog_field', which the issue links. 'vendors': every directory under AlpacaCore/src/vendors/, mapped to the SDK and document names it is built from ('tracked') or to a 'no_upstream' reason. --check fails on an SDK without 'updates', a docs-only directory with neither a document under it nor a no_upstream entry, an unmapped vendor directory, and a workflow ver= pin the snapshot does not read. 'doc_only': directories that hold protocol documents, udev rules or other non-package files. Update this file when a directory under AlpacaCore/external/ is added, removed or its SDK is bumped (then run --pin; --check fails until you do) (docs/development.md, 'Dependency graph').",
